#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:194
msgid ""
"TMEM is a dedicated on-chip memory introduced in Blackwell GPUs, designed to "
"reduce register pressure and enable asynchronous, single-threaded MMA "
"operations. It is organized as a 2D array of 512 columns by 128 rows "
"(lanes), with each cell being 32 bits. Allocation is performed in units of "
"columns, and every lane of a column is allocated together."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:196
msgid "Key properties and requirements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:197
msgid "The number of columns allocated must be a power of 2 and at least 32."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:198
msgid ""
"TMEM allocations are dynamic. TileLang deallocates them automatically at the "
"end of the allocation block unless you call ``T.deallocate_tmem`` to take "
"manual control of the lifetime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:201
msgid "Both allocation and deallocation must be performed by the same warp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:202
msgid ""
"The base address of the TMEM allocation is stored in shared memory and used "
"as the offset for TCGEN5.MMA accumulator tensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:203
msgid ""
"Only TCGEN5.MMA and specific TMEM load/store instructions can access TMEM; "
"all pre-processing must occur before data is loaded into TMEM, and all post-"
"processing after data is retrieved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:204
msgid ""
"The number of columns allocated should not increase between any two "
"allocations in the execution order within the CTA."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:206
msgid ""
"Logical buffer shape.  The last two modes are the matrix modes; any leading "
"modes are batch dimensions that repeat the buffer along TMEM columns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:210
msgid "Element data type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:213
msgid ""
"A TVM buffer object allocated in TMEM scope, suitable for use as an "
"accumulator or operand in TCGEN5.MMA operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:218
msgid ""
"TMEM is only available on supported architectures (e.g., Blackwell and "
"later)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:219
msgid ""
"The buffer returned should be used according to TMEM access restrictions. "
"Use ``T.deallocate_tmem`` only when you need an earlier, explicit release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:229
msgid ""
"The reducer lives in the virtual ``local.reducer`` scope and may only be "
"accessed through the epoch operations::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:232
msgid ""
"acc = T.alloc_reducer(shape, dtype, op=\"sum\")\n"
"T.reducer_init(acc)          # or T.reducer_init(acc, init_value)\n"
"for ...:\n"
"    T.reducer_update(acc[indices], contribution)\n"
"dst = T.alloc_fragment(shape, dtype)\n"
"T.finalize_reducer(acc, dst)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/allocate/index.rst:239
msgid ""
"Ordinary reads/writes, ``T.clear``/``T.fill``, aliasing, and in-place "
"finalize are rejected at compile time. Physical storage and the cross-thread "
"communication plan are chosen by the compiler; the physical layout can never "
"change how many times a logical contribution is combined."
msgstr ""

